# SECTION 05 — MANUAL WORD-LEVEL ANNOTATION

Create a genuine human-verifiable word-timestamp reference dataset.

Use Praat/TextGrid or another technically equivalent annotation system where justified.

Do not confuse forced alignment with ground truth.

A forced aligner predicts boundaries.

A ground-truth annotation establishes the manually verified reference boundaries.

These are not equivalent.

## 5.1 Annotation Requirements

For the timestamp evaluation subset, annotate:

- Word text.
- Start time.
- End time.
- Speaker identity where known.
- Language per word where relevant.
- Disfluency events.
- Repetition events.
- Annotation uncertainty.

Maintain verbatim speech.

Example:

```text
Audio:
"من من فکر می‌کنم که این موضوع مهمه."

Correct word sequence:
من | من | فکر | می‌کنم | که | این | موضوع | مهمه
```

Do not delete the repetition.

Do not correct grammar.

Do not rewrite informal Persian into formal Persian.

Preserve the spoken lexical content.

## 5.2 TextGrid Structure

Design an annotation format with a consistent mapping to the benchmark schema.

A possible TextGrid design:

```text
Tier: speaker
Tier: words
Tier: language
Tier: disfluency_events
Tier: repetition_events
Tier: annotation_uncertainty
```

Adapt tier types and naming to actual Praat capabilities.

Use interval tiers for word boundaries.

Create validation tooling that checks:

```text
word_start >= 0
word_end > word_start
word_end <= audio_duration
```

Check chronological consistency and overlapping intervals.

Where overlapping speech occurs, preserve legitimate speaker overlap rather than incorrectly rejecting the recording.

## 5.3 Annotation Quality

Where multiple annotators are available, independently annotate at least 20% of the timestamp evaluation subset.

Measure:

- Boundary agreement.
- Word transcription agreement.
- Disagreement distribution.
- Adjudication outcomes.

Use median and P90 boundary disagreement as annotation-quality indicators.

Target inter-annotator boundary disagreement:

```text
MEDIAN_ABSOLUTE_DISAGREEMENT <= 50 ms
P90_ABSOLUTE_DISAGREEMENT <= 150 ms
```

These are annotation quality targets, not model performance measurements.

If human annotation is required but unavailable in the execution environment:

- Build the complete annotation workflow.
- Create the audio assignment package.
- Create annotation instructions.
- Create validation scripts.
- Prepare the Praat/TextGrid import/export process.
- Identify samples requiring manual review.
- Do not mark those samples manually annotated without actual human verification.

Do not let unavailable manual annotation prevent all other independent work.

